<report>
<line><title>Spearman's rank correlation</title></line>
<line></line>
<line><in>sample_1</in> vs. <in>sample_2</in></line>
<line>Observations per sample = <in>obs</in></line>
<line>Spearman's score = <in>ix</in></line>
<line></line>
<line>Spearman's rank correlation coefficient (Rho) =  <in>rho</in></line>
<line></line>
<block name="noci"><line><warnabit>CI not calculated when rho is 1 or -1.</warnabit></line></block>
<block name="ci"><line><ci><in>pc</in>% CI for rho (Fisher's Z transformed) = <in>from</in> to <in>to</in></ci></line></block>
<block name="lown">
<line></line>
<line><warnabit>Can not consider probability with very small samples (n &lt; 4)</warnabit></line></block>
<block name="results">
<block name="nop"><line><warnabit>P not calculable</warnabit></line></block>
<block name="results">
<line></line>
<line><pval>Upper side <in>p_u</in></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: positive correlation)</line>
<line><pval>Lower side <in>p_l</in></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: negative correlation)</line>
<line><pval>Two sided <in>p_2</in></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: any correlation)</line>
</block>
</block>
<block name="ties">
<line></line>
<line><warnabit>Ties present: exact P not used</warnabit></line>
</block>
</report>
